1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:10,360
This is a video demonstrating how to work on ASW. 

2
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:20,360
First, enable admin access so you can access the tool.

2
00:00:37,360 --> 00:01:12,670
After that, open the Ascet tool, 

3
00:01:14,670 --> 00:01:25,670
then import the databases that were loaded from TCM.

3
00:01:41,670 --> 00:01:46,960
These are the databases loaded from TCM.

3
00:01:51,670 --> 00:01:58,960
We will take the item name and search for it in the component name section. 

4
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:25,700
After having found the item, check whether the version is correct.

5
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:40,350
Then create the ATT and a test environment folder for that item.

5
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,350
This step creates the necessary files.

6
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:25,660
These files are used for the Alinoe tool. 

6
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:30,660
Create the ATT folder for the item,

6
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:20,660
Then find the missing parameter variables.

7
00:05:25,660 --> 00:05:30,890
Continue searching until all missing Parameters have been found.

8
00:05:54,890 --> 00:05:59,390
Search for the missing Formula after adding the Parameters.

9
00:07:08,810 --> 00:07:15,370
Import the Formula that was exported.

9
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:37,510
After completing the ATT folder creation step.

10
00:07:37,510 --> 00:07:43,230
Next, we will use the Alinoe tool to create the test design.

11
00:08:37,230 --> 00:08:44,520
Create the necessary files in the ATT folder of the item.

12
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:48,620
This is required so that GenTestDesign can be used.

13
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:51,470
After that, fill in the required information fields into the Alinoe tool.

14
00:09:52,470 --> 00:09:55,450
This is needed to generate the test design, 

16
00:09:55,450 --> 00:10:10,860
module name, version, sequence number, the folder where the module will be created and the location that contains the test design.

17
00:10:12,860 --> 00:10:20,960
After that, import the DCM file that was exported earlier.

18
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:23,660
Then run GenTestDesign.

19
00:10:30,660 --> 00:10:34,740
After checking the Min, Max, and Mid fields,

20
00:10:34,740 --> 00:10:38,740
and the necessary information of the variables in the class,

21
00:10:38,740 --> 00:10:42,360
we will search for the missing information

22
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:49,460
in order to add the Local Parameter variables into Alinoe tool.

23
00:11:07,460 --> 00:11:15,480
Proceed to check the Min, Max, Tolerance values of the input variables.

25
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:32,040
Proceed to find the missing Min, Max, Mid, and tolerance values for the Imported Parameter variables.

26
00:14:47,140 --> 00:14:51,960
Check whether the formulas of the Local Parameter variables are correct.

27
00:15:21,660 --> 00:15:24,650
After that, proceed to enter the Input.

28
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:45,940
Write the formula for the Return Value variables.

29
00:16:13,780 --> 00:16:17,460
Then click Generate Test Case to create the test design.

30
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:02,880
The test design has been created successfully.

31
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:47,420
After having created the test design, we will create the test cases to cover C0, C1 and MCDC.

32
00:17:52,420 --> 00:18:05,740
Because this test request only requires C0 and C1, we will only create test cases to cover C0 and C1.

33
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:22,430
This is the basic information tab of the Class.

34
00:18:22,430 --> 00:18:29,180
It includes the review source, tester, and the C0, C1 and MCDC percentages of the Class.

35
00:18:39,180 --> 00:18:48,180
Next, we will import the test cases from the test design into the ATT folder.

36
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:34,000
We will use the Smart ATT tool to import the test cases from the test design into the ATT folder.

37
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:50,640
Fill in the required information into the tool so the test cases can be imported.

38
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:17,730
After importing the test cases into ATT, we will run a trial to check whether the C0, C1 result of the module or item has reached 100%.

39
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:43,460
These are the test cases that were added from the test design into ATT.

40
00:26:32,220 --> 00:26:42,440
This is the result table showing the C0, C1 and MCDC percentages for the item.

41
00:27:46,440 --> 00:27:55,860
After the result has passed, copy the folder from the ATT_Temp into the workspace folder.

42
00:28:44,860 --> 00:28:49,800
After that, create the PLT folder for the item.

43
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:25,150
After the PLT folder is created, we will proceed to color the variables.

44
00:31:25,150 --> 00:31:31,360
After coloring for the PLT file is complete, we will send the result to TCM.

45
00:32:46,360 --> 00:33:01,050
As this item does not require MCDC, so for the conditions required for MCDC coverage, we will select the reason as "MCDC is not required".

46
00:33:47,020 --> 00:33:50,880
After that, we will send the result to TCM.

47
00:41:50,820 --> 00:42:00,400
After sending is complete, we will create a walkthrough for the item.

47
00:43:30,820 --> 00:43:34,400
Fill in the required fields in the MCDC tool to create walkthrough.

48
00:44:42,400 --> 00:44:51,370
After filling in all the information in the make walkthrough MCDC tool, we will create walkthrough for the item.

49
00:44:58,370 --> 00:45:06,090
Next is the step of getting the link on TCM. 

49
00:45:30,370 --> 00:45:36,090
Currently, after the result has been sent, the status is shown as Complete.

50
00:45:36,090 --> 00:45:46,780
However, UT result has not been uploaded to TCM yet, we can reload the database to check again.

51
00:49:08,780 --> 00:49:19,230
After checking that the version on TCM matches the UT design version that I sent to TCM, we will get the link to create the walkthrough.

52
00:52:09,230 --> 00:52:19,870
Once the walkthrough is created, we will proceed to upload the walkthrough to TCM.
